# `/public/uploads` WITHOUT the trailing slash, so the rule covers a SYMLINK too.
# With the slash it matched only a directory, and `artisan serve` serves `public/` while the
# application's `theme` disk writes to the REPO ROOT `uploads/` (all 337 tracked upload files are
# there, none under public/) -- so a dev environment needs `public/uploads -> ../uploads` to see
# what the app uploaded, and that symlink was showing up as untracked and could have been
# committed by a `git add -A`. The intent of this rule has always been "never track public
# uploads"; this makes it hold for the symlink as well.
/public/uploads

# `/public/storage` for the SAME reason, and because it was TRACKED until 2026-11-24 -- at mode
# 100755, holding 62 bytes of the vendor's own build path (`/var/www/html/Product/EcommerceGo/...`).
# A symlink serialised as text by the WorkDo release packaging. So in every checkout `public/storage`
# was a FILE, nothing under `/storage/...` resolved (30 views and 24 PHP files use `Storage::url`),
# and `php artisan storage:link` printed "The [public/storage] link already exists." and changed
# nothing -- the documented remedy defeated by the committed file. Laravel's own shipped .gitignore
# ignores this path; so does the `/public/uploads` rule above, for the same per-environment reason.
# Each environment runs `php artisan storage:link` once.
/public/storage

# The DEV FIXTURE's own uploads. `database/seed-p2dev.php` creates store 1 and writes its images
# to the repo-root `uploads/` where the application's `theme` disk really writes, and a browser
# test that uploads a cover image lands there too. Store 1 exists only in a developer's local
# database -- NOTHING under `uploads/1/` is tracked, while 407 files under other store ids are --
# so these are regenerable test artefacts, not product content, and a `git add -A` must not sweep
# them into a commit. Ignored by store id rather than by filename because the seeder and the
# browser tests use different naming.
/uploads/1/

# THE SAME ARTEFACTS AT THE DOUBLED PREFIX, which is where the application REALLY writes them.
# `Utility::upload_file()` and `keyWiseUpload_file()` prepend `uploads/` to a `$dir` their callers
# already build as `uploads/<store id>`, so a product cover image or gallery image for store 1
# lands at `uploads/uploads/1/` -- not at `uploads/1/`, which the rule above covers.
# `StoredPathPolicy::resolve()` already documents that doubled prefix and peels it before reading
# the tenant segment. Found when the F196/F199 bite runs -- which deliberately let the upload
# branch execute -- left two files there that `git status` reported as untracked and a `git add -A`
# would have committed. 105 files under OTHER store ids are tracked at this path and stay tracked.
/uploads/uploads/1/

# AND THE FIXTURE IS NO LONGER ONE STORE, SO THE TWO RULES ABOVE DO NOT COVER IT.
# Measured 2026-11-26: `seed-p2dev.php` creates TWO stores -- id 1 `Damascus Textiles` AND id 2
# `Aleppo Soap Co` -- so a fixture rebuild writes cover and gallery images under `uploads/2/` and
# `uploads/uploads/2/` as well, which the store-1 rules let straight through. 156 such files were
# found untracked after this session's agents drove real screens against the fixture.
#
# THERE IS DELIBERATELY NO `/uploads/2/` RULE, and adding one would be a defect. Store 2 is also a
# REAL store id: 188 files are tracked at `uploads/2/` and 84 at `uploads/uploads/2/`, product
# content that a blanket ignore would mask the next genuine addition to. The fixture's artefacts
# there are `*_cover.jpg` and `*_one.jpg` and are regenerable, so they must be DELETED rather than
# ignored. Deleting the 156 left the tracked count at 407, unchanged, and none of their names
# collided with a tracked file -- check both before removing any more.
/vendor/
/node_modules/

# Keep the storage/ directory TREE in version control (.gitkeep placeholders) while
# ignoring its CONTENTS. Previously the blanket `/storage/` rule meant a fresh clone
# had no storage/ at all, so the application could not boot from source.
/storage/*
!/storage/app/
/storage/app/*
!/storage/app/public/
/storage/app/public/*
!/storage/framework/
/storage/framework/*
!/storage/framework/cache/
/storage/framework/cache/*
!/storage/framework/cache/data/
/storage/framework/cache/data/*
!/storage/framework/sessions/
/storage/framework/sessions/*
!/storage/framework/testing/
/storage/framework/testing/*
!/storage/framework/views/
/storage/framework/views/*
!/storage/logs/
/storage/logs/*
!.gitkeep
/public/storage

# Secrets must never be committed again. .env is already in history (commit 3c39c160)
# and its credentials must be treated as compromised and rotated; this rule only stops
# it recurring. .env.testing is tracked ON PURPOSE: it holds no secret and it is what
# stops the suite falling back to .env.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.testing

# Artefacts that should never have been committed.
/error_log
composer.phar
/_active', 1)
.DS_Store

# PHPUnit's per-run cache. Regenerated on every run and machine-specific; it has no
# business in version control and shows up as an untracked file after any test run.
.phpunit.result.cache
.phpunit.cache

# Personal Claude Code configuration; project configuration is .claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Written by the vendored paytabscom/laravel_paytabs package (not by this repository) into the
# application root whenever a PayTabs code path runs, which the Feature suite does. Regenerated on
# every run, so it shows up as an untracked file and makes the tree look dirty after any test run.
/debug_paytabs.log

# P2: the local dev database the screenshot harness seeds (database/seed-p2dev.php builds it).
# Never committed: it is a database, and the repository has a standing rule against those.
database/p2dev.sqlite

# Python bytecode from docs/design-system/tools (a mutation test imported the
# checker as a module and left a .pyc, which got committed once -- 50529d6b).
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# =================================================================================================
# DATABASE DUMPS AND ARCHIVES -- recurrence containment for P1-SEC-40 (issue #120). 2026-11-11.
# =================================================================================================
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING IT FIXED ANYTHING. These patterns stop the NEXT dump from being
# committed. `storesyria_ecommercego.sql` was untracked from the working tree on 2026-11-11
# (`git rm --cached`), which is why *.sql now covers it -- `git check-ignore` reports a tracked
# path as NOT ignored, so this block was inert against it until that removal. The blob stays
# fetchable from history regardless: the only true remediation of the git channel is a history
# rewrite, which this project forbids without a separate owner authorization. The plan for it is
# docs/security/P1-SEC-40-INCIDENT.md section 6.
#
# What that dump contains, measured 2026-11-11 by counting patterns, never printing values:
# 29,790 rows across 84 tables (198 tables exist in the schema; 84 carry data). 93 bcrypt hashes
# -- customers 57, users 33, delivery_boys 2, lynomia_contact_verifications 1. Email addresses in
# 14 tables, led by shetabit_visits 186, order_billing_details 143, stores 34. 6,442 raw visitor
# request rows carrying headers, user agents and referers. 7 personal_access_tokens rows (4 User,
# 2 DeliveryBoy, 1 Customer), every one with ["*"] abilities -- stored as SHA-256 digests with
# zero plaintext tokens present, so the dump hands over no usable bearer token.
# Gateway keys present are Stripe TEST mode. Zero matches for sk_live_, pk_live_, AKIA, AIza,
# ghp_, SendGrid or Slack tokens, and zero for `base64:`, so no APP_KEY is inside the dump
# itself. That is NOT reassurance about APP_KEY generally: per CLAUDE.md it is in git history and
# unrotated, and the live host serves .git (see docs/security/P1-SEC-40-INCIDENT.md section 3).
*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.dump
*.bak

# Phase 03 dev-only: /themes resolves from the repo root in production (docroot == repo root),
# so this bridge exists for `php artisan serve` alone and must never be committed.
/public/themes

# PHASE 03 M3-D. The storefront fixture's 44 synthetic tiles, same pattern as `/uploads/1/` above
# and for the same reason. They WERE committed under the repository-root `uploads/` tree, and the
# first Phase 03 CI run refused them: `.htaccess:33-36` rewrites `/uploads/...` to
# `public/uploads/...` only when the file does NOT exist at the root, so a committed one is served
# directly by the webserver with no application and no authorisation (P1-OWN-10, owner decision 11).
#
# The bytes now live in `docs/development/phase-3/fixtures/media/` -- outside anything served -- and
# `docs/development/phase-3/tools/seed-storefront-fixture.php` copies them here when a developer
# seeds. Note `public/uploads` is a SYMLINK to this same directory (see the top of this file), so
# these rules cover both spellings of the destination.
/uploads/p3fixt/
/uploads/2/p3fixt/
/uploads/5/p3fixt/
/uploads/6/p3fixt/

# GAP-274. The two store folders the image-variant tests write REAL files into.
#
# `ImageVariants` resolves through `realpath(base_path(...))` and `gd` reads and writes with
# ordinary file functions -- the `Storage` facade is not in that path at all -- so `Storage::fake()`
# would put the fixture where `base_path()` cannot see it and every assertion would be satisfied by
# "the original was not found". The tests therefore write into `base_path('uploads')`, under store
# ids no store has, and remove them in `tearDown()`; each also asserts in `setUp()` that its folder
# did not already exist, so a leftover cannot make a later run read a previous one's files. These
# two rules are insurance against a crashed run leaving artefacts staged.
/uploads/987321/
/uploads/987654/

# Workflow-tool git worktrees. These are live checkouts created by the Workflow tool for
# isolated subagents; they are embedded git repositories and must never be committed.
.claude/worktrees/
